IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part V, sections 30 to 37: a corporation's
-- holding of its own shares (30 to 33), the purchase and redemption of its own shares and the solvency
-- tests that limit them (34 to 36), and a gift of a share (37). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. The "holding body
-- corporate" and "subsidiary body corporate" of the text are the keel's definitions (s 2(4), s 2(5)); here a
-- fact is asked about the body in question. The prescribed conditions and consequences of s 31(4) to (6)
-- are in regulations that are not among the sources: whether they were met is a plain input.
-- The solvency tests of s 34(2), s 35(3) and s 36(2) read the shared record
-- `Facts for a solvency test in Part V` from cb1-nouns.l4. Each reads only the fields it names.

§ `Part V -- A corporation's own shares (s 30 to s 37)`

§§ `s 30 the general rule`

-- s 30(1)(a): "shall not hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate", "subject to subsection
-- (2) and sections 31 to 36". The holding is permitted where one of the exceptions applies.
-- src:523 | 30 (1) Subject to subsection (2) and sections 31 to 36, a corporation
-- src:524 | (a) shall not hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate; and
-- src:525 | (b) shall not permit any of its subsidiary bodies corporate to acquire shares of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 30(1) corporation holding its own shares (src:523-525)
GIVEN `section 31(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 31(2) permits the corporation to hold the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 32(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate within s 30(1)(a)` MEANS
        `section 31(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares`
    OR  `section 31(2) permits the corporation to hold the shares`
    OR  `section 32(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares`

-- s 30(1)(b): "shall not permit any of its subsidiary bodies corporate to acquire shares of the corporation",
-- subject to s 31(3) and s 31(4).
-- src:523 | 30 (1) Subject to subsection (2) and sections 31 to 36, a corporation
-- src:524 | (a) shall not hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate; and
-- src:525 | (b) shall not permit any of its subsidiary bodies corporate to acquire shares of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 30(1) corporation holding its own shares (src:523-525)
GIVEN `section 31(3) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 31(4) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may permit a subsidiary body corporate to acquire shares of the corporation within s 30(1)(b)` MEANS
        `section 31(3) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares`
    OR  `section 31(4) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares`

-- s 30(2): "Subject to section 31, a corporation shall cause a subsidiary body corporate of the corporation
-- that holds shares of the corporation to sell or otherwise dispose of those shares within five years from
-- the date (a) the body corporate became a subsidiary of the corporation; or (b) the corporation was
-- continued under this Act." If both have happened the five years run from the later (fork cb1-F8 in
-- NOTES.md); a corporation that was not continued has only (a).
-- NOTHING: section 31 permits the holding, so there is no duty to dispose.
-- src:527 | (2) Subject to section 31, a corporation shall cause a subsidiary body corporate of the corporation that holds shares of the corporation to sell or otherwise dispose of those shares within five years from the date
-- src:528 | (a) the body corporate became a subsidiary of the corporation; or
-- src:529 | (b) the corporation was continued under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 30(2) subsidiary holding shares of its parent (src:527-529)
DECIDE `the five-year limit of s 30(2)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 5
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:527 | (2) Subject to section 31, a corporation shall cause a subsidiary body corporate of the corporation that holds shares of the corporation to sell or otherwise dispose of those shares within five years from the date
-- src:528 | (a) the body corporate became a subsidiary of the corporation; or
-- src:529 | (b) the corporation was continued under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 30(2) subsidiary holding shares of its parent (src:527-529)
GIVEN `section 31 permits the subsidiary to hold the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the body corporate became a subsidiary of the corporation` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation was continued under this Act, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for the subsidiary to dispose of the shares within s 30(2)` MEANS
    IF `section 31 permits the subsidiary to hold the shares`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day the corporation was continued under this Act, if it was`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the last day of` `the five-year limit of s 30(2)` `counted from` `the day the body corporate became a subsidiary of the corporation`)
         WHEN JUST continued THEN
             JUST (`the last day of` `the five-year limit of s 30(2)` `counted from` (IF continued AT LEAST `the day the body corporate became a subsidiary of the corporation` THEN continued ELSE `the day the body corporate became a subsidiary of the corporation`))

§§ `s 31 exceptions: what a corporation and its subsidiaries may hold`

-- s 31(1): "in the capacity of a personal representative ... unless it or the holding body corporate or a
-- subsidiary of either of them has a beneficial interest in the shares".
-- src:531 | 31 (1) A corporation may in the capacity of a personal representative hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate unless it or the holding body corporate or a subsidiary of either of them has a beneficial interest in the shares.
@ref CBCA s 31(1) exception (src:531)
GIVEN `the corporation holds the shares in the capacity of a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation, the holding body corporate or a subsidiary of either of them has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 2(4) (keel)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 31(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` MEANS
        `the corporation holds the shares in the capacity of a personal representative`
    AND (NOT `the corporation, the holding body corporate or a subsidiary of either of them has a beneficial interest in the shares`)

-- src:533 | (2) A corporation may hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money.
@ref CBCA s 31(2) idem (src:533)
GIVEN `the corporation holds the shares by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is for the purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 31(2) permits the corporation to hold the shares` MEANS
        `the corporation holds the shares by way of security`
    AND `the security is for the purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money`

-- src:535 | (3) A corporation may permit any of its subsidiary bodies corporate to acquire shares of the corporation
-- src:536 | (a) in the subsidiary’s capacity as a personal representative, unless the subsidiary would have a beneficial interest in the shares; or
-- src:537 | (b) by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money.
@ref CBCA s 31(3) exception -- subsidiary acquiring shares (src:535-537)
GIVEN `the subsidiary acquires the shares in its capacity as a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary would have a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary acquires the shares by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is for the purposes of a transaction entered into by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 31(3) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares` MEANS
        (    `the subsidiary acquires the shares in its capacity as a personal representative`
         AND (NOT `the subsidiary would have a beneficial interest in the shares`))
    OR  (    `the subsidiary acquires the shares by way of security`
         AND `the security is for the purposes of a transaction entered into by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money`)

-- s 31(4): "through the issuance of those shares by the corporation to the subsidiary body corporate if,
-- before the acquisition takes place, the conditions prescribed ... are met".
-- src:539 | (4) A corporation may permit any of its subsidiary bodies corporate to acquire shares of the corporation through the issuance of those shares by the corporation to the subsidiary body corporate if, before the acquisition takes place, the conditions prescribed for the purposes of this subsection are met.
@ref CBCA s 31(4) exception -- conditions precedent (src:539)
GIVEN `the subsidiary acquires the shares through their issuance by the corporation to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(4) were met before the acquisition took place` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 31(4) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares` MEANS
        `the subsidiary acquires the shares through their issuance by the corporation to it`
    AND `the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(4) were met before the acquisition took place`

-- src:541 | (5) After an acquisition has taken place under the purported authority of subsection (4), the conditions prescribed for the purposes of this subsection must be met.
@ref CBCA s 31(5) conditions subsequent (src:541)
GIVEN `an acquisition has taken place under the purported authority of subsection 31(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(5) are met` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conditions subsequent of s 31(5) are satisfied` MEANS
    `an acquisition has taken place under the purported authority of subsection 31(4)`
    IMPLIES `the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(5) are met`

-- s 31(6): the prescribed consequences apply "notwithstanding subsections 16(3) and 26(2)". Which they are
-- is prescribed; the rule says whether they apply.
-- src:543 | (6) If
-- src:544 | (a) a corporation permits a subsidiary body corporate to acquire shares of the corporation under the purported authority of subsection (4), and
-- src:545 | (b) either
-- src:546 | (i) one or more of the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection (4) were not met, or
-- src:547 | (ii) one or more of the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection (5) are not met or cease to be met,
-- src:548 | then, notwithstanding subsections 16(3) and 26(2), the prescribed consequences apply in respect of the acquisition of the shares and their issuance.
@ref CBCA s 31(6) non-compliance with conditions (src:543-548)
GIVEN `the corporation permitted a subsidiary body corporate to acquire shares of the corporation under the purported authority of subsection 31(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more of the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(4) were not met` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `one or more of the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(5) are not met or cease to be met` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the prescribed consequences apply to the acquisition and issuance within s 31(6)` MEANS
        `the corporation permitted a subsidiary body corporate to acquire shares of the corporation under the purported authority of subsection 31(4)`
    AND (    `one or more of the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(4) were not met`
          OR `one or more of the conditions prescribed for the purposes of subsection 31(5) are not met or cease to be met`)

§§ `s 32 Canadian ownership`

-- s 32(1): "Subject to subsection 39(8)", a corporation may hold shares in itself, for the purpose of
-- assisting itself or an affiliate or associate to qualify under a prescribed law for benefits by reason of a
-- specified level of Canadian ownership or control, that (a) are not constrained for that purpose or (b)
-- are shares into which shares held under (a) were converted that are constrained and were not previously
-- held by the corporation.
-- src:550 | 32 (1) Subject to subsection 39(8), a corporation may, for the purpose of assisting the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under any prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control, hold shares in itself that
-- src:551 | (a) are not constrained for the purpose of assisting the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to so qualify; or
-- src:552 | (b) are shares into which shares held under paragraph (a) were converted by the corporation that are constrained for the purpose of assisting the corporation to so qualify and that were not previously held by the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 32(1) exception relating to Canadian ownership (src:550-552)
GIVEN `the purpose is to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under a prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the shares are not constrained for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are shares into which shares held under paragraph 32(1)(a) were converted by the corporation, are constrained for that purpose and were not previously held by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 39(8) forbids the corporation to hold them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 32(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` MEANS
        `the purpose is to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under a prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control`
    AND (    `the shares are not constrained for that purpose`
          OR `the shares are shares into which shares held under paragraph 32(1)(a) were converted by the corporation, are constrained for that purpose and were not previously held by the corporation`)
    AND (NOT `subsection 39(8) forbids the corporation to hold them`)

-- src:554 | (2) A corporation shall not transfer shares held under subsection (1) to any person unless the corporation is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the ownership of the shares as a result of the transfer would assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to achieve the purpose set out in subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 32(2) prohibited transfers (src:554)
GIVEN `the corporation is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the ownership of the shares as a result of the transfer would assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to achieve the purpose set out in subsection 32(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may transfer the shares held under subsection 32(1) within s 32(2)` MEANS
    `the corporation is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the ownership of the shares as a result of the transfer would assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to achieve the purpose set out in subsection 32(1)`

-- src:556 | (3) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with subsection (2) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@ref CBCA s 32(3) offence (src:556)
GIVEN `the corporation fails to comply with subsection 32(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 32(3)` MEANS
        `the corporation fails to comply with subsection 32(2)`
    AND (NOT `the corporation has reasonable cause`)

-- src:556 | (3) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with subsection (2) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@ref CBCA s 32(3) offence (src:556)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose on a corporation on summary conviction within s 32(3)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING

-- s 32(4): a director who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced "is a party to and guilty of the
-- offence", "whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted".
-- src:558 | (4) Where a corporation commits an offence under subsection (3), any director of the corporation who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 32(4) directors of corporation (src:558)
GIVEN `the corporation commits an offence under subsection 32(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 32(4)` MEANS
        `the corporation commits an offence under subsection 32(3)`
    AND `the person is a director of the corporation`
    AND `the director knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

-- src:558 | (4) Where a corporation commits an offence under subsection (3), any director of the corporation who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 32(4) directors of corporation (src:558)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose on a director on summary conviction within s 32(4)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- s 32(5): where shares held under (1) are transferred, s 25(1), (3), (4) and (5), paragraph 115(3)(c) and
-- s 118(1) apply "as if the transfer were an issue".
-- src:560 | (5) Where shares held under subsection (1) are transferred by a corporation, subsections 25(1), (3), (4) and (5), paragraph 115(3)(c) and subsection 118(1) apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of the transfer as if the transfer were an issue.
@ref CBCA s 32(5) where shares are transferred (src:560)
GIVEN `the shares were held under subsection 32(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are transferred by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transfer is treated as an issue of shares within s 32(5)` MEANS
        `the shares were held under subsection 32(1)`
    AND `the shares are transferred by the corporation`

-- src:562 | (6) No transfer of shares by a corporation shall be void, voidable or, in Quebec, null solely because the transfer is in contravention of subsection (2).
@ref CBCA s 32(6) transfer not void, voidable or null (src:562)
GIVEN `the transfer contravenes subsection 32(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is void, voidable or null on a ground other than that it contravenes subsection 32(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transfer of shares is void, voidable or null within s 32(6)` MEANS
    `the transfer is void, voidable or null on a ground other than that it contravenes subsection 32(2)`

§§ `s 33 voting shares`

-- src:564 | 33 (1) A corporation holding shares in itself or in its holding body corporate shall not vote or permit those shares to be voted unless the corporation
-- src:565 | (a) holds the shares in the capacity of a personal representative; and
-- src:566 | (b) has complied with section 153.
@ref CBCA s 33(1) voting shares (src:564-566)
GIVEN `the corporation holds shares in itself or in its holding body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it holds the shares in the capacity of a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has complied with section 153` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 153 (piece cb3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shares may be voted or permitted to be voted within s 33(1)` MEANS
    `the corporation holds shares in itself or in its holding body corporate`
    IMPLIES (    `it holds the shares in the capacity of a personal representative`
             AND `it has complied with section 153`)

-- src:568 | (2) A corporation shall not permit any of its subsidiary bodies corporate holding shares in the corporation to vote, or permit those shares to be voted, unless the subsidiary body corporate satisfies the requirements of subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 33(2) subsidiary body corporate (src:568)
GIVEN `the subsidiary body corporate holds shares in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary body corporate satisfies the requirements of subsection 33(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the subsidiary may vote or be permitted to vote the shares within s 33(2)` MEANS
    `the subsidiary body corporate holds shares in the corporation`
    IMPLIES `the subsidiary body corporate satisfies the requirements of subsection 33(1)`

§§ `s 34 to s 36 purchase and redemption of shares; solvency`

-- s 34(2): no payment to purchase or otherwise acquire shares "if there are reasonable grounds for believing
-- that (a) the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become
-- due; or (b) the realizable value of the corporation's assets would after the payment be less than the
-- aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes". For an open-end mutual fund the stated
-- capital provisions do not apply (s 26(11)), so its stated capital term is nil (fork cb1-F9 in NOTES.md).
-- src:572 | (2) A corporation shall not make any payment to purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it if there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:573 | (a) the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:574 | (b) the realizable value of the corporation’s assets would after the payment be less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes.
@ref CBCA s 34(2) limitation (src:572-574)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for a solvency test in Part V`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is forbidden to make the payment to acquire its shares within s 34(2)` MEANS
        facts's `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
    OR  facts's `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` LESS THAN (facts's `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars`) PLUS (IF facts's `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` THEN 0 ELSE facts's `stated capital of all classes, in dollars`)

-- s 34(1): "Subject to subsection (2) and to its articles, a corporation may purchase or otherwise acquire
-- shares issued by it."
-- src:570 | 34 (1) Subject to subsection (2) and to its articles, a corporation may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it.
@ref CBCA s 34(1) acquisition of corporation's own shares (src:570)
GIVEN `the articles forbid the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 34(2) forbids the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it within s 34(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the articles forbid the acquisition`)
    AND (NOT `subsection 34(2) forbids the payment`)

-- src:576 | 35 (1) Notwithstanding subsection 34(2), but subject to subsection (3) and to its articles, a corporation may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it to
-- src:577 | (a) settle or compromise a debt or claim asserted by or against the corporation;
-- src:578 | (b) eliminate fractional shares; or
-- src:579 | (c) fulfil the terms of a non-assignable agreement under which the corporation has an option or is obliged to purchase shares owned by a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation.
-- src:580 | Idem
-- src:581 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection 34(2), a corporation may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it to
-- src:582 | (a) satisfy the claim of a shareholder who dissents under section 190; or
-- src:583 | (b) comply with an order under section 241.
@ref CBCA s 35(1), s 35(2) alternative acquisition of corporation's own shares (src:576-583)
DECLARE `Purpose of an acquisition of the corporation's own shares (s 35)` IS ONE OF
    `to settle or compromise a debt or claim asserted by or against the corporation`
    `to eliminate fractional shares`
    `to fulfil the terms of a non-assignable agreement under which the corporation has an option or is obliged to purchase shares owned by a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation`
    `to satisfy the claim of a shareholder who dissents under section 190`
    `to comply with an order under section 241`
    `any other purpose`

-- s 35(1) and s 35(2): "Notwithstanding subsection 34(2)". Paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) are "subject to subsection
-- (3) and to its articles"; (2)(a) and (b) say neither, so the articles and (3) do not restrain them.
-- src:576 | 35 (1) Notwithstanding subsection 34(2), but subject to subsection (3) and to its articles, a corporation may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it to
-- src:577 | (a) settle or compromise a debt or claim asserted by or against the corporation;
-- src:578 | (b) eliminate fractional shares; or
-- src:579 | (c) fulfil the terms of a non-assignable agreement under which the corporation has an option or is obliged to purchase shares owned by a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation.
-- src:580 | Idem
-- src:581 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection 34(2), a corporation may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it to
-- src:582 | (a) satisfy the claim of a shareholder who dissents under section 190; or
-- src:583 | (b) comply with an order under section 241.
@ref CBCA s 35(1), s 35(2) alternative acquisition of corporation's own shares (src:576-583)
GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose of an acquisition of the corporation's own shares (s 35)`
      `the articles forbid the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 35(3) forbids the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may purchase or acquire shares issued by it for the purpose within s 35(1) and s 35(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `to settle or compromise a debt or claim asserted by or against the corporation` THEN (NOT `the articles forbid the acquisition`) AND (NOT `subsection 35(3) forbids the payment`)
    WHEN `to eliminate fractional shares` THEN (NOT `the articles forbid the acquisition`) AND (NOT `subsection 35(3) forbids the payment`)
    WHEN `to fulfil the terms of a non-assignable agreement under which the corporation has an option or is obliged to purchase shares owned by a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation` THEN (NOT `the articles forbid the acquisition`) AND (NOT `subsection 35(3) forbids the payment`)
    WHEN `to satisfy the claim of a shareholder who dissents under section 190` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to comply with an order under section 241` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other purpose` THEN FALSE

-- s 35(3): a payment under (1) is forbidden if there are reasonable grounds for believing (a) inability to
-- pay liabilities, or (b) that the realizable value of the assets would be less than the aggregate of the
-- liabilities and "the amount required for payment on a redemption or in a liquidation of all shares the
-- holders of which have the right to be paid before the holders of the shares to be purchased or acquired,
-- to the extent that the amount has not been included in its liabilities".
-- src:585 | (3) A corporation shall not make any payment to purchase or acquire under subsection (1) shares issued by it if there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:586 | (a) the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:587 | (b) the realizable value of the corporation’s assets would after the payment be less than the aggregate of
-- src:588 | (i) its liabilities, and
-- src:589 | (ii) the amount required for payment on a redemption or in a liquidation of all shares the holders of which have the right to be paid before the holders of the shares to be purchased or acquired, to the extent that the amount has not been included in its liabilities.
@ref CBCA s 35(3) limitation (src:585-589)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for a solvency test in Part V`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is forbidden to make the payment to acquire its shares under s 35(1) within s 35(3)` MEANS
        facts's `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
    OR  facts's `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` LESS THAN (facts's `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars`) PLUS (facts's `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars`)

-- s 36(1): "Notwithstanding subsection 34(2) or 35(3), but subject to subsection (2) and to its articles", purchase
-- or redeem redeemable shares "at prices not exceeding the redemption price thereof stated in the articles or
-- calculated according to a formula stated in the articles".
-- src:591 | 36 (1) Notwithstanding subsection 34(2) or 35(3), but subject to subsection (2) and to its articles, a corporation may purchase or redeem any redeemable shares issued by it at prices not exceeding the redemption price thereof stated in the articles or calculated according to a formula stated in the articles.
@ref CBCA s 36(1) redemption of shares (src:591)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemable shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price paid per share, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the redemption price per share stated in the articles or calculated according to a formula stated in the articles, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the articles forbid the redemption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 36(2) forbids the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may purchase or redeem the shares at the price within s 36(1)` MEANS
        `the shares are redeemable shares`
    AND `the price paid per share, in dollars` AT MOST `the redemption price per share stated in the articles or calculated according to a formula stated in the articles, in dollars`
    AND (NOT `the articles forbid the redemption`)
    AND (NOT `subsection 36(2) forbids the payment`)

-- src:593 | (2) A corporation shall not make any payment to purchase or redeem any redeemable shares issued by it if there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:594 | (a) the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:595 | (b) the realizable value of the corporation’s assets would after the payment be less than the aggregate of
-- src:596 | (i) its liabilities, and
-- src:597 | (ii) the amount that would be required to pay the holders of shares that have a right to be paid, on a redemption or in a liquidation, rateably with or before the holders of the shares to be purchased or redeemed, to the extent that the amount has not been included in its liabilities.
@ref CBCA s 36(2) limitation (src:593-597)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for a solvency test in Part V`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is forbidden to make the payment to purchase or redeem redeemable shares within s 36(2)` MEANS
        facts's `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
    OR  facts's `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` LESS THAN (facts's `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars`) PLUS (facts's `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid rateably with or before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars`)

§§ `s 37 gift or legacy of shares`

-- src:599 | 37 A corporation may accept from any shareholder a share of the corporation surrendered to it as a gift including, in Quebec, a legacy but may not extinguish or reduce a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on any such share except in accordance with section 38.
@ref CBCA s 37 gift or legacy of shares (src:599)
GIVEN `the share is surrendered to the corporation by a shareholder as a gift, or in Quebec as a legacy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may accept the share within s 37` MEANS
    `the share is surrendered to the corporation by a shareholder as a gift, or in Quebec as a legacy`

-- src:599 | 37 A corporation may accept from any shareholder a share of the corporation surrendered to it as a gift including, in Quebec, a legacy but may not extinguish or reduce a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on any such share except in accordance with section 38.
@ref CBCA s 37 gift or legacy of shares (src:599)
GIVEN `the corporation extinguishes or reduces a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on the share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so in accordance with section 38` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may extinguish or reduce the liability within s 37` MEANS
    `the corporation extinguishes or reduces a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on the share`
    IMPLIES `it does so in accordance with section 38`
